{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le01ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n2le01ob07re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob07re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Julian</strong>: Good Morning! </br>\n<strong>Caroline</strong>: Good Morning. Please have a sit. So, you are here for our programming assistant teacher job, right? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: Yes, ma'am.  </br>\n<strong>Caroline</strong>: Can I have your CV? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: Here you are! </br>\n<strong>Caroline</strong>: Ok, can I ask you some questions? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: Sure. </br>", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob07re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: Can you tell me what language syntax is? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: Well, everything you have to know is that a computer language describes the possible combination of some symbols that define legal programs. You need to consider this information when you have a structured document or piece of data. </br>\n<strong>Caroline</strong>: When do you use it? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: You can use language syntax in all programming languages. Also, it has some specific rules that depend on various factors, for example, the purposes of its use and the way programmers execute the document or data. </br>\n<strong>Caroline</strong>: How can you explain this matter in a classroom? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: Well, I can say that language syntax is usually a combination of expressions or tokens to specify the categories and characters from which programs are created. </br>", "time": "21000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob07re2img03.jpg", "text": "<strong>Caroline</strong>: Does language syntax have any distinctive features? </br>\n<strong>Julian</strong>: Some basic features of a language's syntax are associated with sequence levels. The first one is related to words that regulate how characters generate tokens; It usually focuses on the lexical analysis. Another is related to phrases that form something we called grammars. It organizes sequences of tokens into a hierarchical syntax tree. The third refers to the context that determines what object names refer to and if they are valid. </br>\n<strong>Caroline</strong>: Ok, your explanation is very impressive indeed. We'll analyze your CV and we'll call you soon. So far, there is nothing else we can do.", "time": "76000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can understand the concept of language syntax. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can exchange information about language syntax. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can identify key features related to language syntax.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you consider the structure of sentences important? Why?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What structural characteristics do you think programming languages have in common?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's learn about language syntax.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0, 