information in a Venn diagram and I explain to my partners language syntax and semantics similarities and differences. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "CV", "type": "name"}, {"content": "it is the abbreviation of the term 'Curriculum Vitae', this refers to a summary of the life of a person", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(acronym)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you have your CV?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "syntax ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the correct arrangement of words in a sentence", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Can you tell me what language syntax is?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "regulate ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the activity of writing computer program", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The first one is related to words that regulate how characters generate tokens.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "distinctive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "It is when something is peculiar or specific", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well\u2026  Does language syntax have any distinctive features?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "token", "type": "name"}, {"content": "it is the basic component of a computer program with different functions according to the programming rules", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Well, I can say that language syntax is usually a combination of expressions or tokens to specify the categories and characters from which programs are created.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "matter ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "it is the subject or that people study in a course", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How can you explain this matter in a classroom?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Indefinite Pronouns: Everything, Nothing, Some", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use <strong>Indefinite pronouns</strong> to refer to people or things in general; this is, you don't specify who or what they are.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are different <strong>Indefinite Pronouns</strong>. to refer to people or things. When we refer to people we use the ending <strong>body</strong> or <strong>one</strong>; Use the ending <strong>thing</strong> if you are talking about objects. The most common indefinite pronouns are everything, nothing, and something (for objects); and everbody, no one and someone (for people)<br><br>  For example: <br> <strong>Everything</strong> is in the bag. <br><br>  Remember that you do not use any negative indicator when you have the indefinites nobody (no one) or nothing in your sentence.</br> Examples: </br>  There is <strong>nothing</strong> I can teach you. </br> There's <strong>no one</strong> here.</br></br> When you use <strong>Indefinite Pronouns </strong>you use a <strong>singular verb</strong> after the pronoun. <br><br> For example: <br> \u2022\tEverybody <strong>has</strong> a computer. <br> \u2022\t<strong>Nothing</strong> is ready for the project. <br><br> You can also add <strong>-'s</strong> to an indefinite when you use a possessive. <br><br> For example:     <br> \u2022\tThe students are in <strong>somebody's</strong> house. <br> \u2022\tIs this <strong>anybody's</strong> laptop? <br><br> In the next chart you can see some examples of indefinite pronouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"anybody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"anyone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"anything\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everybody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"nobody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"none\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everybody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"everything\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"no one\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"someone\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"somebody\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"something\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"all\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"another\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"any\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"both\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"neither\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"many / much\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"several\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Less / little\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Well, everything you have to know is that a computer language describes the possible combination of some symbols that define legal programs.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Also, it has some specific rules that depend on various factors.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Another, is related to phrases that shape something that we called grammars.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Modal Can for Ability to Talk about Language Syntax", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the modal verb <strong>can </strong>or <strong>can't </strong> in the negative from, to talk about abilities or inabilities.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Use the modal verb <strong>can</strong> and its negative form <strong>can't </strong>to express the abilities, or lack of abilities, of a person, animal, or thing. <strong>Can</strong> is a modal verb; that means, can doesn't have any particular conjugation. Can is always the same to all pronouns. </br>Example:</br>He can program computers.</br>I can program computers too.</br></br>Can doesn't need an auxiliary verb neither; if you want to mention an inability, you just add the particle <i>not</i> to the verb can or use the contracted verb <strong>can't</strong>.</br>Examples:</br> We <strong>cannot</strong> understand the grammar. </br> He <strong>cannot</strong> read grammars.</br></br>You always use a verb in <strong>infinitive</strong> with no prepositions after can. </br>Example: </br>We can <strong>read</strong> the statements. </br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"CAN\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"infinitive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"program.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"can\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Design.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "You can use language syntax in all programming languages. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Well, I can say that language syntax is usually a combination of expressions or tokens to specify the categories and characters from which programs are created.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}]}